  "term": "pursuit rotor",
  "definition": "A pursuit rotor is a tracking task used to assess visuomotor performance, in which a person tries to keep a cursor centered on a moving target using manual controls. Better pursuit-rotor performance reflects more accurate continuous tracking of a moving object.",
